(Stage 1d — a `value` parameter among enough arguments to spill to the
 stack. Here there are 6 parameters: 5 numbers (words 0-4) and 1 value
 (words 5,6). That is 7 argument words, so the value's TAG word (word 6)
 is the 7th word and lands on the stack at [rbp+16] while its payload is
 in r9 — the register/stack straddle. Acceptance 3.)

To "classify7" with a number called "a" and a number called "b" and a number called "c" and a number called "d" and a number called "e" and a value called "v".
  If v is a text, print "text".
  Otherwise print "number".

"classify7" of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and "hello".
"classify7" of 1 and 2 and 3 and 4 and 5 and 6.